COMPONENTS, TYPES & FUNDAMENTALS
--------------------------------
Voltage class     : 110 kV  (line-to-line, 3-phase AC)
Typical frequency : 50 / 60 Hz
Typical current   : hundreds of A to a few kA
BIL (impulse)     : ~550 kV
Clearance (phase) : ~1.1–1.5 m air, more with pollution

Bus pipes
  Type        : rigid aluminium or copper tubular bus
  Role        : low-impedance interconnection of bays
  Variable    : I²R heating, skin effect, short-circuit force

Insulators
  Types       : porcelain or polymer (composite) post / string
  Role        : support live parts, isolate from earth
  Variable    : creepage distance, pollution class, CIGRE flashover

Cables
  Types       : XLPE or oil-filled HV cable
  Role        : connection from overhead bus to apparatus
  Variable    : capacitance, charging current, sheath voltage

Bushings
  Types       : condenser / RIP / OIP
  Role        : insulated penetration into breaker tank
  Variable    : tan δ, partial discharge, oil level (if OIP)

Oil circuit breaker (shown)
  Type        : bulk-oil or minimum-oil tank CB
  Role        : interrupt load and fault current
  Variables   : breaking current (kA), arcing time, oil dielectric
  Note        : older technology; many 110 kV yards now use SF6 or vacuum

Regular circuit breaker
  Type        : often SF6 live-tank or dead-tank at 110 kV today
  Role        : same as above — isolate and quench arc
  Variables   : rated short-circuit current, TRV, operating time

Fence / yard
  Role        : personnel safety, animal barrier
  Fundamentals: step & touch voltage, earth-grid design, gravel resistivity

ADDITIONS: typical 110 kV yard
  Power transformers (110/33 kV or 110/11 kV) — the actual “transformation”
  Current & voltage transformers (CTs / VTs)
  Surge arresters
  Isolators / disconnectors
  Earthing switches
